# --------------------------------------------------------------- Runtime data
# Scan results and the per-installation identity are generated at runtime and
# are specific to whoever ran the tool. They must never be committed: the
# identity is what keeps one installation's scans out of another's view, and
# shipping one would give every clone the same one.
data_store/
*.log
ecdat_config.json
zypher_config.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Vendored binary
# OpenGrep is ~52 MB. It is fetched during setup rather than committed, so the
# repository stays clonable on a slow connection and the history does not carry
# a binary that changes wholesale on every upgrade. Its LICENSE and NOTICE.md
# are tracked, because the obligations are ours whether the binary is here or
# not. See the README for how to install it.
vendor/opengrep/*
!vendor/opengrep/LICENSE
!vendor/opengrep/NOTICE.md

# -------------------------------------------------------- Submission material
# Competition deliverables. They describe the project rather than build it, and
# they carry team-identifying detail, so they are kept out of the public repo.
*.pptx
*.pdf
*.docx
SIH_details.md

# ------------------------------------------------------- Local scan fixtures
# Deliberately weak cryptography used to exercise the scanners. Harmless, but a
# repository full of hardcoded keys and MD5 calls trips secret scanners and
# teaches the wrong thing to anyone who reads it out of context.
test/

